; ============================================================
; TITLE:    Pie Chart
; CATEGORY: Mathematics
; LEVEL:    Intermediate
; TAGS:     data, charts, percentages, angles, filled
; SUMMARY:  Draws a pie chart from a list of data, with each slice sized by its share of 360 degrees.
; ============================================================
;
; WHAT IT DOES
;   Shows how a school day of 24 hours is spent. Every activity gets
;   a slice of the pie. The angle of the slice is its fraction of the
;   whole, times 360 degrees. Percentages are written next to the
;   slices and a key on the right names the colors.
;
; HOW TO USE
;   Press Run. Edit the list "day at the bottom to chart something
;   else. The numbers do not have to add up to 100 or 24: the program
;   adds them up itself and works out each share.
;
; CONCEPTS YOU WILL LEARN
;   * fractions of a whole turned into angles and percentages
;   * SIN and COS to find points on a circle
;   * FILLED with a path made of many short straight lines
;   * keeping a running total (the angle where the next slice starts)
;
; THINGS TO TRY
;   * Add [Music 1] to the list and watch every slice shrink a little.
;   * Change :radius, or move the pie by changing :cx and :cy.
;   * Print the angle of each slice as well as its percentage.
; ============================================================

make "cx -120
make "cy 0
make "radius 200
make "colors [[230 80 70] [250 170 50] [90 180 90] [70 140 220] [160 100 200] [240 120 170] [120 200 210]]

; The point on the rim at a given angle. Angles here are compass
; style, like turtle headings: 0 is straight up and they go clockwise.
to rim :angle :r
  output list :cx + :r * sin :angle :cy + :r * cos :angle
end

; One slice from angle :a1 to angle :a2. The edge of the pie is
; made of many little straight steps, one per degree, which is
; close enough to a curve that nobody can tell.
to slice :a1 :a2 :color
  penup setxy :cx :cy
  filled :color [
    setpos rim :a1 :radius
    for (list "a :a1 :a2 1) [setpos rim :a :radius]
    setpos rim :a2 :radius
    setxy :cx :cy
  ]
  ; a white line between slices makes them easier to tell apart
  setpencolor "white setpensize 3
  pendown setpos rim :a1 :radius penup
end

to pie :data
  localmake "total reduce "sum map [last ?] :data
  localmake "start 0
  setlabelheight 15
  foreach :data [
    localmake "angle 360 * (last ?) / :total
    localmake "color item 1 + remainder (# - 1) count :colors :colors
    slice :start :start + :angle :color
    ; the percentage sits just outside the middle of the slice
    setpencolor [50 50 50]
    setpos rim :start + :angle / 2 :radius + 28
    setx xcor - 14 sety ycor - 5
    label word round 100 * (last ?) / :total "%
    key # first ? :color
    make "start :start + :angle
  ]
end

; One line of the color key on the right of the screen.
to key :n :name :color
  penup setxy 170 150 - 34 * :n setheading 0
  filled :color [repeat 4 [forward 20 right 90]]
  setxy 200 ycor + 4
  setpencolor [50 50 50] label :name
end

clearscreen hideturtle
make "day [[Sleep 9] [School 7] [Play 3] [Meals 2] [Homework 1] [Reading 2]]
pie :day
penup setxy -260 260 setpencolor "black setlabelheight 22
label [How I spend a school day]
